Check why ArgoCD pods are failing

Run:

Shell
kubectl describe pod argocd-redis-86d4d669f7-qq8b5 -n argocd

Check logs:

Shell
kubectl logs argocd-redis-86d4d669f7-qq8b5 -n argocd
Check Node Status
Shell
kubectl get nodes

Should show:

Plain Text
minikube Ready
Restart ArgoCD Pods
Shell
kubectl delete pod --all -n argocd

Kubernetes will recreate them automatically.

Watch:

Shell
kubectl get pods -n argocd -w

Wait until all become:

Plain Text
1/1 Running
If still not healthy

Restart deployments:

Shell
kubectl rollout restart deployment -n argocd

Restart StatefulSet:

Shell
kubectl rollout restart statefulset argocd-application-controller -n argocd
 
Verify ArgoCD Service
Shell
kubectl get svc -n argocd

Then start port forwarding:

Shell
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443

Open:

Plain Text
https://localhost:8080
